Subject: [PATCH] ARM: dts: qcom: matisse3g: match the WLAN DXE level IRQs

The driver programs both DXE IRQs as level-high on startup. Describing them
as rising edges prevents subsequent probing: the existing GIC mapping
rejects the mismatched firmware specification with -ENXIO. Match the mode
that is already used by the working driver on this board.


---
diff --git a/arch/arm/boot/dts/qcom/qcom-msm8226-samsung-matisse3g.dts b/arch/arm/boot/dts/qcom/qcom-msm8226-samsung-matisse3g.dts
--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/qcom/qcom-msm8226-samsung-matisse3g.dts
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/qcom/qcom-msm8226-samsung-matisse3g.dts
@@ -244,8 +244,8 @@
 
 				wifi {
 					compatible = "qcom,wcnss-wlan";
-					interrupts = <GIC_SPI 145 IRQ_TYPE_EDGE_RISING>,
-						     <GIC_SPI 146 IRQ_TYPE_EDGE_RISING>;
+					interrupts = <GIC_SPI 145 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>,
+						     <GIC_SPI 146 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
 					interrupt-names = "tx", "rx";
 					qcom,smem-states = <&apps_smsm 10>, <&apps_smsm 9>;
 					qcom,smem-state-names = "tx-enable", "tx-rings-empty";
